      "text": "I am a one-person business in South Africa. Here is my branding:\n\nBusiness name: [NAME]\nTagline: [TAGLINE or \"none\"]\nOne-sentence description: [PASTE]\nLogo: [DESCRIBE IT IN DETAIL, or attach the image]\nColours: [HEX CODES]\nTypefaces: [NAMES]\nVoice: [THREE WORDS]\n\nCritique this honestly. Do not be encouraging. Assume I can take it.\n\nGo through each of these and answer plainly:\n\n1. Does any part of this look AI-generated or template-made? Point at\n the specific element and say why.\n2. Would this still work if a competitor put their name on it? If yes,\n which parts?\n3. What visual cliché from my industry am I repeating without realising?\n4. Where will this break: small sizes, one colour, embroidery, a vehicle,\n a black and white print?\n5. Which text-on-background pairs look risky for readability? I will\n check the exact contrast ratios myself at webaim.org, so do not\n claim to have calculated them.\n6. Does the name, tagline and description all say the same thing, or do\n they contradict each other?\n7. What is the single weakest element, and what would you replace it with?\n8. Was any part of this generated by an image tool rather than set in a\n real font or drawn? If so, tell me which parts I may struggle to own\n or protect, and what to redo by hand.\n\nEnd with the three changes that would improve this most, in order of\nimpact. Be specific. Do not suggest a full redesign.",
